  "notes": [
   "Breadboard rows f-j are drawn in the upper half of the image and mapped to bank 'b'; rows a-e (lower half) are bank 't', following the catalogue naming.",
   "Column positions are estimated from the image: resistor 3b.g to 6b.g, LED anode (bent leg) at 6b.h and cathode at 8b.h, blue wire from pin 9 to 3b.f, black wire from GND to 8b.g.",
   "The pot's centre (wiper) pin is at column 23 and its side pins at columns 22 and 24 (the pot straddles the centre gap). Yellow wire to A0 shares the strip 23b with the wiper. Red wire from 5V goes to column 24 (VCC) and black wire from GND to column 22 (GND).",
   "The two GND wires use GND.1 (digital header) and GND.2 (power header). Exact GND pin assignments are arbitrary because all GND pins are common.",
   "The LED's longer, positive leg (anode) is on the resistor side, as the text says."
